WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:10.491
Thuan: One for you… one for you… and one
for you!

2
00:00:16.341 --> 00:00:17.683
All full!

3
00:00:18.983 --> 00:00:20.183
[door chimes]

4
00:00:29.633 --> 00:00:32.452
[paper rips]
Tetsuo: Hahahaha!

5
00:00:33.552 --> 00:00:35.742
[record scratch]
Thuan: Hey! What are you doing?!

6
00:00:36.292 --> 00:00:37.254
Tetsuo: Ahem.

7
00:00:38.904 --> 00:00:40.219
Thuan: Come back here!

8
00:00:40.819 --> 00:00:42.019
[door chimes]

9
00:00:46.769 --> 00:00:47.837
[thud]
Got it!

10
00:00:48.387 --> 00:00:49.669
[birds tweeting]
Tetsuo: …Ahem.

11
00:00:57.019 --> 00:01:01.832
Nhung: Thuan? Oh dear. That is a big tear.

12
00:01:02.082 --> 00:01:06.864
Thuan: Tetsuo tore it off! And I've only
got this little bit of tape.

13
00:01:07.114 --> 00:01:10.531
Nhung: Is that enough? Or do you need a
new roll from my shop?

14
00:01:10.781 --> 00:01:12.206
Thuan: I have no idea.

15
00:01:12.856 --> 00:01:13.856
[time stops]

16
00:01:13.856 --> 00:01:19.336
Johansson: Two sisters, one torn poster,
and a question about tape. Let us measure

17
00:01:19.336 --> 00:01:20.510
it for them.

18
00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:26.040
Thirty centimetres along the top. Forty
down the side.

19
00:01:26.890 --> 00:01:31.574
Most people would simply add them: thirty
plus forty, seventy.

20
00:01:31.824 --> 00:01:37.774
But that is the way round the corner. The
tear cuts straight across, so it must be

21
00:01:37.774 --> 00:01:38.124
shorter.

22
00:01:38.974 --> 00:01:43.948
The corner is a right angle, so the torn
piece is a right-angled triangle.

23
00:01:44.198 --> 00:01:47.953
Square each side. Thirty squared is nine
hundred.

24
00:01:48.203 --> 00:01:50.850
Forty squared is sixteen hundred.

25
00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:57.231
Add them: twenty-five hundred. And the
square root of twenty-five hundred is

26
00:01:57.231 --> 00:01:57.692
fifty.

27
00:01:57.942 --> 00:02:02.244
And on her roll there is… exactly fifty
centimetres of tape.

28
00:02:02.494 --> 00:02:05.713
Exactly enough. She just doesn't know it
yet.

29
00:02:06.913 --> 00:02:10.357
[time starts again]
Thuan: Let's just try… It fits! Exactly!

30
00:02:10.607 --> 00:02:12.050
Nhung: Well, there goes my sale.

31
00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:17.753
Johansson: So that is Pythagoras' theorem.
But why does it work?

32
00:02:18.003 --> 00:02:23.614
Take four copies of the torn triangle, and
put them inside one big square.

33
00:02:23.864 --> 00:02:30.735
Like this, the space left over is two
squares: one on each short side.

34
00:02:31.585 --> 00:02:35.002
Now slide the same four triangles around.

35
00:02:35.252 --> 00:02:41.976
The space left over is one tilted square,
on the long side. Same space, so the same

36
00:02:41.976 --> 00:02:42.371
area.

37
00:02:43.221 --> 00:02:47.977
So, for any right angle: square the two
sides, add them, then take the square

38
00:02:47.977 --> 00:02:48.294
root.

39
00:02:48.544 --> 00:02:52.957
A squared plus b squared equals c squared.

